Z||000011||lowCG||10-20-2001||01:07 AM||||The problem,I've found,is that the paint,powder-coat get messed up when the springs are going in and then the rust starts.<BR>A good urethane is as good as a powder coat for keeping the springs from rusting,so just scrape,sand and paint them in the car,unless they're entirely coated with rust already.||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroSTETZ||10-20-2001||02:12 AM||||what about those cans of rubber stuff at home depot that you dip tool handles in?||||reg||1
Z||000013||artherd||10-20-2001||02:33 AM||||I've had good results with powdercoated parts.  If done properly, the finish is nearly indistructable under normal use (however, it will chip if you drop your springs onto a whirling table saw's open <BR>blade for example...)<P>Just be careful installing them!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000014||87ECO5||10-20-2001||11:05 AM||||Won't the powder-coating crack when the springs compress?||||reg||5
Z||000015||grinthock||10-20-2001||11:15 AM||||One of my customers here in Canada is called Metal Koting, they do guess what Metal Coating (Yes the comapny is called Koting!)<P>They do powder coating of stuff like that, might try looking for them, they are a international company, they are <P>Metal Koting - A Division of Continuous Color Coat.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||tomcat06085||10-20-2001||05:01 PM||||Look in a phonebook..yellow pages section for heat treaters and metallurgy...most heat treating or plating shops will do the black oxide or just about any color you want. Call them and ask how they want them prepared for heat sealer or black oxide. Explain what you're doing and they'll generally do it for you if you deliver and pick up. Try the local job shops that do tool & die making.<P>------------------<BR>tomcat<BR>Thanks for the help!||||reg||3
